      "section": "Genotypes, two ways",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "One table, two pictures. Left, the allele grid: a row per donor, a column per locus, each cell split into its two haplotypes and coloured by allele group, so every A*02 shares a hue; a homozygous locus is one merged cell with a dot. Right, an oncoplot of the same rows with the allele as the category: one value per cell, so a heterozygous locus shows only one of its two alleles. Click an allele half to narrow the predictions below to it, a donor name to pick that donor. Input: OptiType calls from nf-core/hlatyping, predictions from nf-core/epitopeprediction.\n",
      "surface": "none",
      "accent": null,
      "logo": null,
      "logo_dark": null,
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
